From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msado15: ADODB.Stream text, charsets, files, lines, CopyTo (2058)

msado15: ADODB.Stream text in its character sets, files, lines and CopyTo.

Text is kept in the stream's Charset (Unicode, UTF-8, ASCII, the
windows-N and iso-8859-N sets, others by their registered names) with the
byte order mark Unicode and UTF-8 text begins with, read and written by
character (the old code wrote a terminating NUL with every text), WriteText
takes adWriteLine and ReadText adReadLine with the LineSeparator, SkipLine
skips a line. Open on a file (a path, URL= or file:), LoadFromFile,
SaveToFile (adSaveCreateNotExist fails over a file), Flush and Close (a
stream opened on a file for writing is written back) and CopyTo work. A
binary Write overwrites at the position instead of growing the stream, and
Position no longer cuts the stream. They were stubs or wrong.
